 "synopsis": "Sahajanand Medical Technologies, a Mumbai-headquartered cardiovascular medical device manufacturer, is launching an initial public offering consisting entirely of an offer for sale of 1.38 crore equity shares. The public subscription opens on October 15 and closes on October 19, with the price band to be announced on October 12. Because the IPO is a pure offer for sale, all proceeds will go to the selling shareholders rather than the company. The selling shareholders include promoters, Samara Capital Markets Holding, Kotak Pre-IPO Opportunities Fund, and NHPEA Sparkle Holding BV. The anchor book opens on October 14, share allotment is expected by October 21, and the stock is scheduled to debut on October 23. Motilal Oswal Investment Advisors, Avendus Capital, HSBC Securities and Capital Markets (India), and Nuvama Wealth Management are managing the IPO.",
